{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>She is my sister, my father's daughter.</b> A father's daughter is permitted to a son of Noah, for fatherhood is not reckoned among gentiles. And in order to confirm his words he answered thus. And if you say — but was she not his brother's daughter? — children of children are like children, and so she is Terach's daughter. And so he says to Lot: ״כִּי אֲנָשִׁים אַחִים אֲנָחְנוּ״ (Genesis 13:8)." "<b>But not my mother's daughter.</b> Haran was from a different mother."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:39.130913487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}